{"id": "75", "question": "The amount of friction and the speed of an object have what kind of relationship?", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): inverse", "B): reverse", "C): direct", "D): equal"], "correct": "A", "initial_cot": "1. Friction is a force that opposes the motion of an object.\n2. The amount of friction depends on the nature of the surfaces in contact and the normal force between them.\n3. The speed of an object is determined by the net force acting on it and its mass.\n4. When the speed of an object increases, the force of friction also increases to oppose the motion.\n5. Therefore, the amount of friction and the speed of an object have a direct relationship.", "initial_cot_probs": [5.310834794158836e-08, 2.2138852528996722e-08, 8.473923662677407e-05, 3.847155483072129e-09], "initial_probs": [0.0003475746780168265, 1.9608820366556756e-05, 6.039942672941834e-05, 5.6180215324275196e-06], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 2, "rt_lambda": 1.0, "cot_step": "Friction is a force that opposes the motion of an object.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Friction is a force that opposes the motion of an object.", "2.", "The amount of friction depends on the nature of the surfaces in contact and the normal force between them.", "3.", "The speed of an object is determined by the net force acting on it and its mass.", "4.", "When the speed of an object increases, the force of friction also increases to oppose the motion.", "5.", "Therefore, the amount of friction and the speed of an object have a direct relationship."], "unlearning_results": {"0": {"completion": "A).\n\nThe amount of friction and", "probs": [0.0003475746780168265, 1.9608820366556756e-05, 6.039942672941834e-05, 5.6180215324275196e-06], "prediction": 0, "target_cot_step": "Friction is a force that opposes the motion of an object.", "target_cot_step_prefix": "Human: Question: The amount of friction and the speed of an object have what kind of relationship?\n\nChoices:\n(A): inverse\n(B): reverse\n(C): direct\n(D